{{Short description|Indonesian traditional food made from beef, sweet potatoes, and corn}}
{{for|the village in Iran|Katamak, Hirmand}}
'''Katemak''' is an [[Indonesian cuisine|Indonesian traditional dish]] from the [[East Nusa Tenggara]] Province. To prepare this dish, [[beef]] is boiled with [[sweet potatoes]], [[sweet corn]] and some green [[vegetables]] such as [[cassava]] leaves and [[papaya]] leaves to make a [[soup]]. Some [[spices]] such as the small [[red onions]], [[garlic]] and [[red chillies]] are added during cooking.<ref>{{in lang|id}} [http://www.sajiansedap.com/recipe/detail/7652/katemak http://www.sajiansedap.com/recipe/detail/7652/katemak] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130731094750/http://www.sajiansedap.com/recipe/detail/7652/katemak |date=2013-07-31 }}, KATEMAK Sajian Sedap</ref>
